@* The folders the service runs tasks in, from server.json (WorkspaceRoots), read only: they are set when the service is
   installed, and a page that could add one could open any folder of the server to a run with a shell. The window's
   add and remove are not offered. *@

<h2 class="label">Writable folders</h2>
<p class="hint">A run may only write inside its workspace, and a workspace of the service is a folder under one of these. They are set when the service is installed - WorkspaceRoots in server.json - and changed there by an administrator of the server, who then restarts the service.</p>

@if (Roots.Count == 0)
{
    <p class="hint">server.json names no folder, so no workspace can be added until it does.</p>
}
else
{
    <ul class="cards settings-roots" aria-label="Workspace roots">
        @foreach (var root in Roots)
        {
            <li class="card"><span class="card-title path">@root</span></li>
        }
    </ul>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The roots as the service has them (ServerSettings.WorkspaceRoots).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<string> Roots { get; set; } = [];
}
